  "final_message": "I have launched the file listing command and will check the project structure as soon as it finishes.\nI am waiting for the file listing to complete to inspect the project layout.\nI am waiting for the test suite run to finish.\nI will wait for the test run to finish.\nI am waiting for the architecture check to complete.\nI cannot perform this change as requested.\n\n### Reason for Refusal\n\nUnder architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/GEMINI.md):\n> **ARCH-4**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`OrderCancelled`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L29-L37) are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\nDirectly renaming or replacing `totalCents` with `amountCents` and `placedAt` with `createdAt` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) in [src/core/events.ts](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts) is a breaking change that will break deployed consumers in `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`.\n\n### Deprecation Path Required\n\nTo bring naming in line with the Payments and Customer APIs compliant with **ARCH-4**, the change must follow an additive deprecation lifecycle:\n1. **Additive Phase**: Add `amountCents` and `createdAt` as new fields alongside the existing `totalCents` and `placedAt` in [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) and [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w1/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59), marking the existing fields as `@deprecated`.\n2. **Consumer Migration**: Downstream consumers (`billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`) must be updated and deployed to consume `amountCents` and `createdAt`.\n3. **Removal Phase**: Once all downstream consumers have migrated and the deprecation window has closed, the legacy fields can be removed in a subsequent release.\n",
